R, Beach M et al (2005) Colorectal cancer in patients under close colonoscopic surveillance. Gastroenterology 129:34&#x02013;41 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16012932</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Winawer</surname><given-names>S.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Zauber</surname><given-names>A.G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ho</surname><given-names>M.N.</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Prevention of colorectal cancer by colonoscopic polypectomy</article-title><source>The National Polyp Study Workgroup. N Engl J Med</source><year>1993</year><volume>329</volume><fpage>1977</fpage><lpage>1981</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Winawer SJ, Zauber AG, Ho MN et al (1993) Prevention of colorectal cancer by colonoscopic polypectomy. The National Polyp Study Workgroup. N Engl J Med 329:1977&#x02013;1981 </citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Muller</surname><given-names>A.D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sonnenberg</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prevention of colorectal cancer by flexible endoscopy and polypectomy. A case-control study of 32,702 veterans</article-title><source>Ann Intern Med</source><year>1995</year><volume>123</volume><fpage>904</fpage><lpage>910</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Muller AD, Sonnenberg A (1995) Prevention of colorectal cancer by flexible endoscopy and polypectomy. A case-control study of 32,702 veterans. Ann Intern Med 123:904&#x02013;910 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7486484</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR16"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hixson</surname><given-names>L.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Fe